{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01550",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.85,
      "end_seconds": 4.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Okay, good morning. I've just opened your notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.26,
      "end_seconds": 9.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Hello. I hope I'm not late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.06,
      "end_seconds": 15.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.44,
      "end_seconds": 21.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair. Where shall we begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.22,
      "end_seconds": 32.87,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "I wanted to get neck pain after a car crash looked at. I told my wife I'd come today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.4,
      "end_seconds": 37.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Alright, has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.61,
      "end_seconds": 45.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "For two weeks, I'd say. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.96,
      "end_seconds": 49.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Is there something that settles it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.65,
      "end_seconds": 54.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "So, I get some relief from heat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.47,
      "end_seconds": 62.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 62.43,
      "end_seconds": 67.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.45,
      "end_seconds": 82.52,
      "duration_seconds": 13.07,
      "text": "I was getting to that! And there's shoulder tightness as well, you know, about three months now. With shoulder tightness, honestly, every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 83.69,
      "end_seconds": 85.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Yes, exactly like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.02,
      "end_seconds": 92.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.61,
      "end_seconds": 97.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "I don't think I have any, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 99.13,
      "end_seconds": 108.1,
      "duration_seconds": 8.97,
      "text": "Actually, I remember she had some kind of reaction to tramadol before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.47,
      "end_seconds": 111.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "I don't remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.27,
      "end_seconds": 119.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "Okay, I'll note both of those. Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.14,
      "end_seconds": 123.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "My uncle has high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.17,
      "end_seconds": 128.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Do you take any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.99,
      "end_seconds": 131.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Nothing regular, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.31,
      "end_seconds": 136.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.12,
      "end_seconds": 143.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "Yes, you know, I had my womb taken out, fifteen years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.11,
      "end_seconds": 147.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.22,
      "end_seconds": 152.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Yes, arthritis in my knees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.7,
      "end_seconds": 153.66,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.33,
      "end_seconds": 169.54,
      "duration_seconds": 14.21,
      "text": "Uh, I've had low haemoglobin for about ten years now. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I've had anxiety for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.63,
      "end_seconds": 180.33,
      "duration_seconds": 9.7,
      "text": "Alright, arthritis in your knees, that matches what I have here. What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.56,
      "end_seconds": 185.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.22,
      "end_seconds": 187.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.13,
      "end_seconds": 192.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.08,
      "end_seconds": 206.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Alright, and what about chest pain or weakness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.01,
      "end_seconds": 220.98,
      "duration_seconds": 11.97,
      "text": "Um, no, no chest pain, no weakness. I did have a headache at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.89,
      "end_seconds": 228.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Have you noticed loss of consciousness or numbness in the arms?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.08,
      "end_seconds": 235.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No, I'd have said so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.56,
      "end_seconds": 241.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.15,
      "end_seconds": 245.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 247.2,
      "end_seconds": 255.89,
      "duration_seconds": 8.69,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Saturation 98 percent, pulse is 84 beats a minute, blood pressure 116 over 75."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.73,
      "end_seconds": 259.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.57,
      "end_seconds": 263.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.47,
      "end_seconds": 265.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.61,
      "end_seconds": 269.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.82,
      "end_seconds": 288.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.88,
      "text": "There is muscle tenderness either side of the neck and no tenderness over the bones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.49,
      "end_seconds": 293.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.17,
      "end_seconds": 320.6,
      "duration_seconds": 9.43,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, it fits best with whiplash-type neck strain. Another possibility is a cervical spine injury."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.3,
      "end_seconds": 323.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.9,
      "end_seconds": 342.26,
      "duration_seconds": 17.36,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like whiplash-type neck strain. We'll begin with naproxen, 500 milligrams, twice a day with food, one week. It's for neck pain. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.19,
      "end_seconds": 347.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}